From: =?UTF-8?q?Mattias=20Walstr=C3=B6m?= <mattias.walstrom@wires.se>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] hostapd: Write the PID file also when not daemonizing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-P only took effect together with -B.  A supervisor running hostapd in
the foreground then has no way to tell when it is ready: write the file
at the point a daemonizing hostapd would, once every interface is up.
It is removed on exit as before.

Signed-off-by: Mattias Walström <mattias.walstrom@wires.se>
---
diff -ruN a/hostapd/main.c b/hostapd/main.c
--- a/hostapd/main.c
+++ b/hostapd/main.c
@@ -592,6 +592,15 @@
 				   strerror(errno));
 			return -1;
 		}
+	} else if (pid_file) {
+		/* Written once every interface is up, like os_daemonize(),
+		 * so the file tells a supervisor that hostapd is ready. */
+		FILE *f = fopen(pid_file, "w");
+
+		if (f) {
+			fprintf(f, "%u\n", getpid());
+			fclose(f);
+		}
 	}
 
 	eloop_run();
